As you can see, we just have a very basic gated check that returns whether we are dealing
with an image. Of course, we're going to need to write that method. Here, we've come to
one of the new C# 8 features that we haven't mentioned yet. Prior to C# 8, the method may
have looked like this:
public static bool IsImage(string fileName)
{
string ext = Path.GetExtension(fileName);
switch (ext)
{
case "png":
case "jpg":
case "jpeg":
case "bmp":
case "gif":
return true;
default: return false;
};
}
However, with the new switch statement, we can write that method like this:
public static bool IsImage(string fileName)
{
string ext = Path.GetExtension(fileName);
return ext switch
{
"png" => true,
"jpg" => true,
"jpeg" => true,
"bmp" => true,
"gif" => true,
_ => false
};
}
We could make it even terser if we included a GetExtension call in the switch statement
itself, but, generally, it reads easier.
The new switch statement is actually more powerful than this and, in
fact, supports pattern matching.
